<article class="env-lemma" id="08AI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08AI">Lemma <span data-tag="08AI">67.20.10</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : Y \to X$ be an affine morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{A} = f_*\mathcal{O}_ Y$. The functor $\mathcal{F} \mapsto f_*\mathcal{F}$ induces an equivalence of categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \left\{  \begin{matrix}  \text{category of quasi-coherent}

\\  \mathcal{O}_ Y\text{-modules} 

\end{matrix} \right\}  \longrightarrow \left\{  \begin{matrix}  \text{category of quasi-coherent}

\\  \mathcal{A}\text{-modules} 

\end{matrix} \right\}   \]
</div>
  <p> Moreover, an $\mathcal{A}$-module is quasi-coherent as an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module if and only if it is quasi-coherent as an $\mathcal{A}$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>